Place them in the repo:


cd ~/your-repo
mkdir -p manifests scripts docs
# Paste the files into their paths
chmod +x scripts/*.sh manifests/02-upf-node-label.sh

Run in order on a fresh VM:


sudo bash scripts/01-host-prepare-hugepages.sh
sudo reboot

# after reboot:
sudo MGMT_IP=192.168.100.200 bash scripts/02-vm-network-setup.sh

sudo bash scripts/03-k8s-prereqs.sh
sudo reboot

# after reboot:
sudo MGMT_IP=192.168.100.200 bash scripts/04-kubeadm-init.sh

# add UPF node label
bash manifests/02-upf-node-label.sh

# now run OnRamp
cd ~/aether-onramp
make aether-pingall
make aether-5gc-install
make aether-gnbsim-install
make aether-gnbsim-run

# validate
sudo bash ~/your-repo/scripts/05-validate-lab.sh

A Few Notes

    The scripts are idempotent where practical — running them twice won't break the system, they'll just skip already-done steps.

    01-host-prepare-hugepages.sh requires a reboot — kernel command line changes never take effect live. It backs up /etc/default/grub before editing.

    02-vm-network-setup.sh moves OnRamp's netplan files aside — this is the specific fix for the "VM becomes unreachable after OnRamp" issue you hit.

    05-validate-lab.sh produces the evidence file you'll want in the repo as validation-evidence.txt — it captures the working state in one reproducible artifact.
